.SS CMT_NO_RESTRICT_FIX
.IP
.EX
#define CMT_NO_RESTRICT_FIX
#include \f[B]\(dqCMT/ATTRIBUTES/RESTRICT.H\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.PP
Define it before the first CMT header to leave the identifier
\f[CR]restrict\f[R] alone, for example in C++ code that uses
\f[CR]restrict\f[R] as a variable or function name.
\f[CR]RESTRICT\f[R] is still defined.
